+| 2026-10-20 | `src/entries/opencode.ts` | The entry registered the v1 hook names (`chat.message`, `tool.execute.before`, `experimental.session.compacting`, `experimental.chat.system.transform`) and called `app.tool(name, def)`. None of those exist in OpenCode 2's plugin API, the v2 loader reads `id`/`setup` off the **default** export, and the entry had no default export at all — so the module could not load under OpenCode 2. | Rewritten against the v2 plugin context: tools register through `ctx.tool.transform(editor => editor.add(...))`; hooks register through `ctx.tool.hook("execute.before"/"execute.after")`, `ctx.session.hook("prompt"/"context"/"compaction")` and `ctx.event.subscribe()`; `cwd` comes from `ctx.location.directory`; the module now default-exports `{id, setup}`. The system payload merges into the last `SystemPart` instead of adding one, so `system.length` is unchanged (#1085). Compaction ownership (`own`/`passthrough`) and the destructive-tool policy are ported from mksglu/context-mode#1194, with the summary text produced inside core (`compactionSummary`) so the entry still never opens context.db. | The v1 names are absent from v2 core: `opencode@1438073 packages/plugin/src/promise/session.ts:138-151` (SessionHooks = prompt, context, compaction), `promise/tool.ts:38-64` (ToolHooks = execute.before, execute.after, registered via `ctx.tool.hook`), `tickets/spike-hooks-verified.md:47` "v1 names are absent from v2 core". `docs/install/opencode.md` and `docs/v2/review/out/final/probe-opencode.md` were both checked against `opencode-ai@1.19.3` — the v1-era plugin API — which is why the probe and this entry disagreed about which API the v2 plugin targets. impl/12 §4 already requires `{id, setup}` and the `ctx.tool.transform`/`editor.add` pattern, so the entry now matches its own spec; the install guide's plugin-file shape is a separate follow-up (it still describes a v1-era `.opencode/plugins/context-mode.js`). |
diff --git a/src/core/hooks/dispatch.ts b/src/core/hooks/dispatch.ts
index 5aac8b5c..7f0c071a 100644
--- a/src/core/hooks/dispatch.ts
+++ b/src/core/hooks/dispatch.ts
@@ -106,6 +106,20 @@ function compactText(db: DbHandle, ev: CanonicalHookEvent, row: AdapterRow): str
   return renderState(readSessionEvents(db, ev.sessionId), ev.turn ?? 0);
 }
 
+// The OpenCode 2 compaction hook owns the summary in "own" mode and needs the text to put in
+// `event.result`, so OpenCode skips its own model summarization call (ported from
+// mksglu/context-mode#1194). The DB stays inside core: the plugin entry never opens context.db
+// (impl/12 §1), so the summary is produced here and handed over as text.
+export async function compactionSummary(project: ProjectContext, sessionId: string, turn: number): Promise<string> {
+  if (sessionId === "") return "";
+  const db = await openDb(project);
+  const rows = readSessionEvents(db, sessionId);
+  // An empty session has nothing to summarise: an empty summary would still suppress the host's own
+  // summarization, so the host is left to do it (ported from mksglu/context-mode#1194).
+  if (rows.length === 0) return "";
+  return renderState(rows, turn);
+}
+
 async function sessionStart(ev: CanonicalHookEvent, row: AdapterRow, project: ProjectContext): Promise<Decision> {
   if (ev.source === "compact" && row.compactDelivery === "sessionstart") {
     const db = await openDb(project);
